# ui-panels.mdc

# UI panels — bold title required

**Panel refactors:** follow step-by-step priorities in [`docs/ui-panel-refactor.md`](../../docs/ui-panel-refactor.md). When the user names a priority (P1–P10), read that section, check off migration steps, and update the progress log.

**Every new or refactored editor panel** (left column, right column, nested sections) must use a **bold title row** from `ui/widgets/panel_header.py`. Do not use `QGroupBox("Title")`, plain `QLabel` panel titles, or the native `QGroupBox` title for the panel name.

## Title helpers

| Helper | When to use |
| ------ | ----------- |
| `create_titled_panel_layout(panel, title, trailing_widgets)` | Title + header buttons (Groups, Layers, Compass `×`, …) |
| `create_simple_titled_panel_layout(panel, title)` | Title only (Palettes, Materials, Selector, Structure, …) |
| `create_nested_group_layout(group, title)` | Nested `QGroupBox` sections (Selected Block, Site grid, Render types, …) |

All three call `add_panel_title_row`, which sets the title `QLabel` font to **bold**.

## Setup checklist for a new panel

1. Subclass `QGroupBox` (or wrap content in a `QGroupBox` inside a column).
2. `super().__init__(parent)` — **no** title string argument.
3. `layout = create_simple_titled_panel_layout(self, "Panel name")` (or `create_titled_panel_layout` if there are header buttons).
4. Add fields and controls to `layout` below the title row.
5. Wire signals in `ui/main_window.py`; document in `docs/ui.md`.

## Do not

- `QGroupBox("My panel")` for the outer or nested section title
- Duplicate title styling in per-panel stylesheets
- Skip the title row on “small” panels (palette, tool hints, settings blocks included)

## Icon buttons (when needed)

- Size: `panel_icon_size()` from `ui/toolbar_icons.py` (18×18).
- Factory: `make_panel_tool_button(icon, tooltip, clicked=...)` from `ui/widgets/panel_tool_button.py`.
- Dismissible panels: `make_panel_close_button` (`assets/ui/window-close.svg`) + `close_requested` signal; add a matching checkable **View** menu action in `ui/main_window.py`.
- Expose actions via **signals**; wire in `ui/main_window.py`.

