- `layer_list_panel.py` / `groups_panel.py` — `create_titled_panel_layout` + four actions
- `properties_panel.py` — nested `create_nested_group_layout` for Selected Block / Grid cell; inspector combo changes live-apply via `brush_inspector_changed` / `brush_blockstate_changed` → `MainWindow._apply_inspector_to_selected_cell` (Signature: `properties-inspector-live-apply`)
- `preview_toolbar.py` — compact `QWidget` row (not a `QGroupBox`); Previous/Next + trailing zoom label for Viewer preview (2D only)
- `orbit_preview_widget.py` — lazy-loaded `QOpenGLWidget` for 3D orbit inside **`_OrbitViewHost`**
  (`preview_panel.py`); created on first **3D** toggle, not at `PreviewPanel` import; `QMatrix4x4.lookAt`
  uses `QVector3D` (Qt6 API). **Free camera (fc0):** `helpers/orbit_camera.py` — eye position +
  azimuth/elevation look; **fc2a (Signature: `floating-camera-fc2a-mouse-look`):** click to capture focus;
  `setMouseTracking(True)` + pointer capture; `BlankCursor` while captured; **Esc** releases; **fc2b
  (Signature: `floating-camera-fc2b-scroll-move-speed`):** scroll/**+**/**−** adjusts fly speed pref
  (not mouse look); transient speed label on **host sibling QLabel** via `move_speed_feedback` — **never**
  child QLabel on GL widget or QPainter in `paintGL` (Signature: `orbit-shader-attribute-blackout`);
  **hold** **WASD** / arrows / Space / Shift via `_movement_timer` (Signature: `floating-camera-fc0-hold-fly`).
  **fc1b (Signature: `floating-camera-fc1b-look-forward`):** W/S/↑/↓ `move_along_look`; A/D/←/→ strafe via
  `move_on_plane` + `cross(forward, up)` right vector — Signature: `floating-camera-fc0-strafe-right`.
  **fc1 reset (Signature: `floating-camera-fc1-reset-projection`):** **R** → `reset_camera_to_default()`;
  near/far clip from `bounds_radius`. **Floating camera HUD (fc3):** top-right 3-line QLabel (`Facing` /
  `Position: X / Y / Z` / `Looking at`); voxel DDA + `format_hud_block_label` → `format_entry_label` for
  materialized catalog names; pref `viewer.orbit_camera_hud` (default on). **Render class:** classify tokens
  with `orbit_render_class()` before editing orbit geometry — Signature: `orbit-render-class-routing`;
  glossary `docs/render-types.md` § Orbit render class. **Partial blocks:** stairs/slabs → opaque atlas
  tiles in `orbit_face_textures.py` (not 2D masks); fences/walls → masked bakes + `sample.a < 0.05` discard
  in `_FRAGMENT_SHADER_TEXTURED`. **C4 attachables:** block-model element faces
  (`orbit_block_model_mesh.py`) — Signature: `orbit-attachable-block-model-faces`. See `docs/render-types.md`
  § lessons learned. **Orbit view host overlays (fc2b):** `#orbit-view-host-overlays` — transient HUD on
  `_OrbitViewHost` sibling, not GL child.

## Structure tab right column (no gaps when hiding)

The right column uses a flat `QVBoxLayout` (`_structure_tools_layout` in `ui/main_window.py`) — **not** a vertical `QSplitter` between inspector and materials.

When adding or removing a panel from that column:

1. `addWidget(panel)` in stack order (tool hints → `_properties_panel` → `_materials_panel`).
2. Register collapsible panels in `_update_structure_tools_column_layout()` (the loop that sets `QSizePolicy.Maximum` on compass, tool hints, and properties).
3. On every show/hide (close button, View menu, tool toggle): call `_update_structure_tools_column_layout()`.
4. Only **one** stretch target: `_materials_panel` when visible; otherwise a bottom `QSpacerItem` pushes panels to the top.

Do **not** give the whole column `stretch=1` on a splitter or container that stays tall when a child is hidden — that recreates empty gaps below Selected Block / Grid cell.

## Structure tab left column (no gaps when hiding)

The left column uses `_palette_column_layout` in `ui/main_window.py`:

1. **Palettes** — only stretch target (`stretch=1`, grows at the top).
2. **Groups**, **Layers**, **Structure** — `QSizePolicy.Maximum`; call `_update_palette_column_layout()` when hiding Structure (close button or **View → Structure settings**).

Do not put `stretch=1` on the bottom panel or a wrapper that stays tall when Structure is hidden.

## Toolbar vs panel

- **Panel** header icons: 18px, `panel_header` + `make_panel_tool_button`.
- **Grid header** toolbar (eraser/save): 22px, `toolbar_icon_size()`, `LayerActionToolbar` / `QToolBar`.
- **Split toolbar buttons** (Selector, Eraser): see `.cursor/rules/ui-split-buttons.mdc`.

## Panel consistency

When creating a new panel:

- Match existing panel spacing
- Match existing title styling
- Match existing icon sizes
- Match existing visibility behavior
- Reuse existing helpers before creating new UI helpers